// REQUIRES: host-linux-amd64 || host-linux-arm64
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-ir-flags.py --self-test | FileCheck %s
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-ir-flags.py --gopp %gopp --root %S --jobs 8 opt/ oom/ | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SCAN
// P04.13, ADR-0028 addendum: LLVM 23.1.0's AArch64 FastISel selects
// `sext (signext i8 arg) to i64` as a zero-extend. The arm64 baseline
// (-pipeline=fastisel) therefore must never contain a sext or trunc of a
// function argument, nor a zext of one wider than i1: the lowering stores an
// argument to its slot first. Both sides: the self-test shows the scan finds
// a hand-made sample with the pattern and accepts one without it; the second
// run scans the narrow-integer and conversion programs (opt/*) on both
// targets (the whole corpus: core-opt-ir-flags.long.test). The same scan
// requires every C allocation function to be declared `nobuiltin` (review
// R6: oom/*, and the self-test with and without the attribute).
//
// CHECK: self-test ok
// SCAN: programs x 2 targets: no flags
